  "body": "All pictures here are licensed as CC0.\n\nHere is a zip file with the out-of-camera RAW and the default processing profile:\n\n[DSCN0165.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24872796/DSCN0165.zip)\n\nHere is the out-of-camera JPEG:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/453d5d90-9f29-46f5-9b9f-285b70150f6e)\n\nHere is the default rendering as provided by ART-1.26.1 on Linux:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e0ec1eb-b50e-4a4a-a8de-f594367af5ea)\n\nAs you see, the colors are badly washed out.\n\nDisabling the tone curve auto-matching fixes colors immediately:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1a1eb40-e522-429f-aa37-0cfacaa38993)\n\nProcessing profile for the above image:\n\n[DSCN0165-corrected-ART.jpg.out.arp.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24872839/DSCN0165-corrected-ART.jpg.out.arp.txt)\n\nIt may be the case that the extreme (but correctable) vignette and barrel distortion of the Nikon Coolpix P1100 lens at its wide end play some role, but I have also seen this on telephoto shots.",
